The rainbows I like best are the ones that appear after a summer shower. The sun comes out, the air smells fresh, and suddenly a bright arc stretches across the sky.

I love the colours: red, orange, yellow, green, blue, indigo and violet. They look like a giant painted ribbon hanging over the rooftops. Sometimes the rainbow is wide and bold, and sometimes it is faint, like a whisper in the sky.

My favourite rainbows are the ones that seem to touch the ground. I imagine a pot of gold hidden at the end, though I know it is only a story. Still, it makes me smile.

Whenever I see a rainbow, I stop and look. It feels like a little gift from the sky, bright and cheerful after the rain. [end of text]


